🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
Today the lookup is a std::find_if call on a map:



      pytorch/torch/csrc/distributed/c10d/symm_mem/NCCLSymmetricMemory.cu


        Lines 296 to 303
      in
      d3aa1dc







           auto alloc_it = std::find_if( 




               allocations_.begin(), allocations_.end(), [&](const auto& pair) { 




                 auto& allocation = pair.second; 




                 auto ptr_int = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(ptr); 




                 auto base_ptr = reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(allocation->ptr); 




                 return ptr_int >= base_ptr && 




                     ptr_int < base_ptr + allocation->buffer_size; 




               }); 





The overhead can be non-negligible.
Alternatives
Action (1):
Establish fast lookup as we did for NVSHMEMSymmetricMemory, using a map from tensor.storage_ptr() to symm_mem handle.
Action (2):
For second level lookup, CUDA has a helper:
CUresult cuMemGetAddressRange(CUdeviceptr* pBase, size_t* pSize, CUdeviceptr ptr);

It can retrieve the base allocation address (and the size) of any device pointer from a CUDA allocation.
Replace the above std::find_if with cuMemGetAddressRange.
