📚 The doc issue
I'm implementing my own memory allocator backend for the XPU device, and doing so via torch.xpu.memory.XPUPluggable allocator. I noticed that every time PyTorch calls my free function, it runs into a segfault.
This is the signature that is given in the XPUPluggableAllocator docstring (I don't know why this doesn't show up on docs.pytorch.org though):
void free_fn(void* ptr, size_t size, sycl::queue* queue);
I'm not super familiar with the source layout, but I did find this call in XPUPluggableAllocator.cpp:
free_fn_(ptr, size, device_idx, queue);
Which lead me to think that the correct signature for the free function is:
void free_fn(void* ptr, size_t size, int device_idx, sycl::queue* queue);
Changing my signature to the above indeed did fix the issue, and I didn't get any segfaults after that.
My free function looks like this (when int device is included in the signature, it works fine):
void torch_free_fn (void * ptr, size_t _size, /*int _device,*/ sycl::queue * q) {
    printf ("Enter free function\n");
    auto queue = *q;  //  <--- Segfault occurs here
    printf ("About to free\n");
    sycl::free (ptr, queue);
    printf ("Freed\n");
}
